# AdGuard Home: ad blocking + local names for your whole network (small LXC)
# A tiny Debian container that runs AdGuard Home directly (no Docker needed).
# Every device on your network asks it for names: ads and trackers get blocked,
# and names like kontor.home.internal point at your apps VM.
# It's a machine of its own on purpose: your network keeps working DNS while the
# apps VM restarts or is being changed.
#
# ask: ADGUARD_REWRITES | Local names | name=ip pairs, e.g. *.home.internal=192.168.1.50. Leave it empty: creating the apps VM adds it here for you.
# ask: ADGUARD_PASSWORD | Web UI password | Empty = generated and saved inside the machine to /root/adguard-admin.txt | secret
# ask: TIMEZONE | Timezone | e.g. UTC, Asia/Riyadh
# next: In your router, set the DHCP DNS server to {ip}, so every device uses it (they pick it up when they reconnect).
# next: AdGuard web UI: http://{ip}/  (user admin; generated password: sudo cat /root/adguard-admin.txt inside it)
#
# Also works on a machine you made yourself:  sudo ./bootstrap.sh -c machines/dns.env
PVE_KIND=lxc
PVE_CORES=1
PVE_MEMORY=512
PVE_DISK=4

ENABLE_ADGUARD=yes
